From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:40:22 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] internal/syscall/windows: pass lpBytesReturned when setting a reparse point

Backported from upstream (CL 744282, commit 93b6475, Go 1.27).

Root.Symlink (CL 660635, commit 26fdb07, Go 1.25) sets a reparse point
through DeviceIoControl with no place for the byte count, and Windows 7
writes the count regardless.

Stop Root.Symlink crashing on Windows 7. Pass a place for the count.

	                       before                 after
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 7              Root.Symlink crashes,  works
	                       exception 0xc0000005
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 8 and later    works                  works

Gate: none | Remembered: N/A

diff --git a/src/internal/syscall/windows/at_windows.go b/src/internal/syscall/windows/at_windows.go
index f12a7f43..11ee7fee 100644
--- a/src/internal/syscall/windows/at_windows.go
+++ b/src/internal/syscall/windows/at_windows.go
@@ -1482,6 +1482,7 @@ func symlinkat(oldname string, newdirfd syscall.Handle, newname string, flags Sy
 	namebuf := rdbbuf[bufferSize:]
 	copy(namebuf, unsafe.String((*byte)(unsafe.Pointer(&oldnameu16[0])), 2*len(oldnameu16)))
 
+	var bytesReturned uint32
 	err = syscall.DeviceIoControl(
 		h,
 		FSCTL_SET_REPARSE_POINT,
@@ -1489,7 +1490,7 @@ func symlinkat(oldname string, newdirfd syscall.Handle, newname string, flags Sy
 		uint32(len(rdbbuf)),
 		nil,
 		0,
-		nil,
+		&bytesReturned,
 		nil)
 	if err != nil {
 		// Creating the symlink has failed, so try to remove the file.
